  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<p>The Carbon Storage Offshore Reference Zones is used to identify Crown land and public pore space in Southwestern Ontario. These zones are used for reference to develop proposals for carbon storage sites under the Geologic Carbon Storage Act, 2025.</p><p>A grid pattern is used to divide the area. 1 zone = 252.81 km2. (18.51km x 13.66km).</p><p><br /><strong>Additional Documentation:</strong><br /><a target='_blank' href='https://www.publicdocs.mnr.gov.on.ca/mirb/Carbon_Storage_Offshore_Reference_Zones_User_Guide.docx' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>User Guide for Carbon Storage Offshore Reference Zones&nbsp;</a></p><p><strong>Status:&nbsp;</strong><br />Completed: production of the data has been completed</p><div><span style='display:inline !important; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px;'><strong>Maintenance and Update Frequency</strong></span></div><div><span style='display:inline !important; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px;'>As needed: Data is updated as deemed necessary</span><br />&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><span style='display:inline !important; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px;'><strong>Contact</strong></span><br />Rebecca Shearon, GIS Officer</div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; max-width:100%; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><ul><li><a href='mailto:rebecca.shearon@ontario.ca' rel='nofollow ugc'><span style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; display:inline !important; line-height:1.5; max-width:100%